WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:17.401
rolled on her skateboard to the top of the concrete ramp, carefully shifting her weight as she came

2
00:00:17.481 --> 00:00:18.061
to a stop.

3
00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.261
"I did it!"

4
00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:24.183
she thought triumphantly, before losing her balance and tumbling backward.

5
00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:28.164
A group of nearby skateboarders laughed.

6
00:00:29.764 --> 00:00:33.485
"Not even close to one of Logan's tricks," one teased.

7
00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:38.086
is Logan?"

8
00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:39.827
Hayley suddenly wondered.

9
00:00:42.627 --> 00:00:48.109
The two of them met at the skate park every Saturday—and he'd promised to help her perfect this

10
00:00:48.229 --> 00:00:48.829
trick today.

11
00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:54.471
She checked her phone, but his last text was from three days earlier.

12
00:00:55.911 --> 00:00:59.372
They'd made plans to meet at the library, but he hadn't shown up.

13
00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:05.332
Instead a text had arrived after midnight: "Sorry.

14
00:01:05.773 --> 00:01:06.574
I forgot."

15
00:01:06.594 --> 00:01:08.896
"Where are you?"

16
00:01:09.336 --> 00:01:10.177
she typed now.

17
00:01:10.197 --> 00:01:12.840
"Is everything okay?"

18
00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:24.852
On Monday in Spanish class, Señora Ramos handed back the students' graded tests.

19
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.343
Hayley felt relieved to see Logan in his seat since she hadn't heard a word from him over

20
00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:31.923
the weekend.

21
00:01:33.484 --> 00:01:40.608
But she also felt irritated that he'd been ditching her so frequently, and today he hadn't even acknowledged

22
00:01:40.648 --> 00:01:42.509
her by waving or anything.

23
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:49.573
She was about to try to catch his eye when she spotted the test on his desk.

24
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:52.474
The grade was shocking.

25
00:01:52.494 --> 00:01:55.336
"Logan got a D?"

26
00:01:55.936 --> 00:01:56.696
Hayley thought.

27
00:01:56.716 --> 00:02:00.698
"What in the world is going on with him lately?"

28
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.281
As the days passed, Hayley rarely saw Logan.

29
00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:10.682
"Is he avoiding me?"

30
00:02:11.242 --> 00:02:11.823
she wondered.

31
00:02:12.923 --> 00:02:15.104
Had she done something to offend him?

32
00:02:16.865 --> 00:02:21.387
She kept checking his online profile, and everything seemed normal.

33
00:02:23.748 --> 00:02:30.653
Then one day she spotted him sitting alone outside at a table near the guidance counselors' offices.

34
00:02:30.673 --> 00:02:35.457
"Hey, Logan," she called, "are you okay?

35
00:02:35.557 --> 00:02:39.240
You haven't been—" "I'm fine," Logan snapped.

36
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.403
Provoked by his tone, Hayley heard herself snapping back.

37
00:02:43.423 --> 00:02:49.008
"There's no need to be so grouchy—I was only asking how you're doing!

38
00:02:49.028 --> 00:02:54.032
I guess you don't care that you're throwing away our friendship with your constant disappearing act.

39
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.361
But if that's what you want, then—" "Ugh!"

40
00:03:00.581 --> 00:03:06.843
Logan got up and stormed off in a huff, leaving Hayley confused, angry, and utterly hurt.

41
00:03:06.863 --> 00:03:09.304
"Is something wrong, Hayley?"

42
00:03:10.824 --> 00:03:11.985
She looked up to see Mr.

43
00:03:12.185 --> 00:03:13.865
Obi, one of the guidance counselors.

44
00:03:13.885 --> 00:03:16.586
"No, I'm fine, but thanks for asking."

45
00:03:16.606 --> 00:03:19.127
"You don't look fine.

46
00:03:20.047 --> 00:03:23.048
But I'm here to listen if you feel like talking," Mr.

47
00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:23.688
Obi said.

48
00:03:25.576 --> 00:03:31.600
As much as Hayley didn't want to talk, she suddenly found herself blurting out all her confusion and

49
00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.861
frustration with Logan.

50
00:03:35.463 --> 00:03:38.305
She was careful, though, to avoid mentioning his name.

51
00:03:39.465 --> 00:03:42.427
Mr. Obi listened quietly until she was finished.

52
00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:48.271
"From what you've told me, it sounds like your friend may be depressed."

53
00:03:49.612 --> 00:03:51.974
A wave of guilt washed over Hayley.

54
00:03:51.994 --> 00:03:54.836
"I didn't think of that."

55
00:03:56.004 --> 00:04:01.647
"Depression is a common condition—in fact, one in five teens experiences it," Mr.

56
00:04:01.727 --> 00:04:02.488
Obi explained.

57
00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:07.050
"People with depression often feel hopeless and irritable.

58
00:04:08.771 --> 00:04:10.892
Their sleep patterns and appetites can change.

59
00:04:12.453 --> 00:04:16.716
They can also have trouble concentrating and may even lose interest in favorite activities.

60
00:04:17.996 --> 00:04:21.278
Sometimes that means they isolate themselves from friends."

61
00:04:24.768 --> 00:04:27.950
"Is there anything I can do for Lo—I mean my friend if he's depressed?"

62
00:04:28.391 --> 00:04:29.111
Hayley asked.

63
00:04:31.493 --> 00:04:33.994
Mr. Obi nodded with a sympathetic smile.

64
00:04:34.014 --> 00:04:39.278
"You can let him know that you care, and you're available to listen.

65
00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:43.401
Try to stay in touch so your friend doesn't feel alone.

66
00:04:45.402 --> 00:04:48.544
If he won't talk to you, encourage him to talk to someone else.

67
00:04:50.085 --> 00:04:54.288
And if you ever think he's in serious trouble, you should let an adult know immediately."

68
00:04:56.472 --> 00:04:57.113
"Thanks, Mr.

69
00:04:57.233 --> 00:04:59.395
Obi—that information is helpful."

70
00:05:00.916 --> 00:05:05.179
Wondering how much time was left before her next class, Hayley checked her phone.

71
00:05:06.721 --> 00:05:12.666
On the screen was a new notification: Logan had posted something on his online profile.

72
00:05:14.107 --> 00:05:18.110
Hayley's hands began to tremble as she showed the counselor her phone.

73
00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:24.476
"Mr. Obi, I think Logan needs help."

74
00:05:28.856 --> 00:05:30.817
"Yes!" Hayley cheered.

75
00:05:32.097 --> 00:05:34.798
She had just executed the new trick perfectly.

76
00:05:35.758 --> 00:05:40.559
Even the skateboarders who usually teased her were impressed, giving her a round of applause.

77
00:05:40.579 --> 00:05:42.380
"Great job!"

78
00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:43.380
someone said.

79
00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.681
"You're here!"

80
00:05:47.061 --> 00:05:49.482
Hayley rolled down the ramp to greet Logan.

81
00:05:49.502 --> 00:05:53.303
"I wasn't sure if you saw my text."

82
00:05:55.444 --> 00:05:56.104
Logan nodded.

83
00:05:58.328 --> 00:06:00.890
"Thanks for staying in touch with me over the last few months.

84
00:06:02.191 --> 00:06:06.335
Mr. Obi reached out too—and recommended that I see a therapist.

85
00:06:08.436 --> 00:06:13.220
I'm feeling better now, except He looked away for a second.

86
00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.603
"Sorry I was a jerk to you."

87
00:06:16.623 --> 00:06:19.585
"No need to apologize!"

88
00:06:20.006 --> 00:06:20.967
Hayley said quickly.

89
00:06:20.987 --> 00:06:24.309
"Do you want to talk about anything?"

90
00:06:26.531 --> 00:06:27.492
Logan shook his head.

91
00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:32.045
"Not really—some stuff just happened at home with my parents."

92
00:06:33.886 --> 00:06:37.107
"Understood. I'm here to listen if you need it."

93
00:06:37.127 --> 00:06:41.649
"Thanks. But for now, how about we just skate?"

94
00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:44.850
he said before hopping on his board to perform a kick flip.

95
00:06:46.751 --> 00:06:50.452
For the first time in weeks, Hayley saw her friend smile.
